---
import { apps, site } from '../data/site';
---
<div class="grid-cards">
  <div class="box" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column">
    <div class="box-head"><span>Step 01</span><span style="color: var(--ink-muted)">Hardware</span></div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <h3 class="h3">Get a radio</h3>
      <p>Most of us started on a Heltec WiFi LoRa 32 V4, the 863–928 MHz version. The wiki keeps a list of boards tested locally.</p>
      <a class="mono" href={site.wikiUrl} style="font-size: 14px; margin-top: 4px">Hardware list →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="box" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column">
    <div class="box-head"><span>Step 02</span><span style="color: var(--ink-muted)">Firmware</span></div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <h3 class="h3">Flash MeshCore</h3>
      <p>Use the official web flasher in Chrome or Edge over USB. Choose companion firmware for your first node.</p>
      <a class="mono" href="/links/" style="font-size: 14px; margin-top: 4px">Find the flasher →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="box" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column">
    <div class="box-head"><span>Step 03</span><span style="color: var(--ink-muted)">App</span></div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <h3 class="h3">Install the app</h3>
      <p>Pair your node over Bluetooth, apply Table 1, set a name and say hello on the public channel.</p>
      <div class="row" style="gap: 10px; margin-top: 6px">
        <a class="btn small" href={apps.android} rel="noopener">Google Play</a>
        <a class="btn small" href={apps.ios} rel="noopener">App Store</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
